      "writtenOn": "2026-10-09T16:00:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Am I reading this correctly that the LUKS passphrase is saved to Juju secret? If so, Juju secret is not assured to be Encryption at Rest, and the big picture here is not to write any secret to the disk unencrypted.\n\nI\u0027m just concerned theoretically that the secret for LUKS device could be leaked to a physical disk without encryption (of the key itself). I hope I\u0027m wrong here though.",
      "revId": "4aa6c36c98ac42f4014de6e755749d446bf816be",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c41c760a_2a2592bd",
        "filename": "charms/openstack-hypervisor/charmcraft.yaml",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 234,
      "author": {
        "id": 38581
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-09T23:00:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for raising this. Just to clarify the lifecycle: the juju secret contains the operator’s existing LUKS passphrase and is only needed during enrollment. Vaultlocker adds a separate managed key stored in Vault, which is used for later unlocks. The intended Sunbeam workflow is to remove the enrollment secret once enrollment is confirmed. That limits how long the passphrase is stored in Juju",
      "parentUuid": "8ffc9ebd_b0a034f2",
      "revId": "4aa6c36c98ac42f4014de6e755749d446bf816be",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4157a882_ade913a5",
        "filename": "charms/openstack-hypervisor/charmcraft.yaml",
